      ∑ u ∈ EuclideanGeometry.distanceSet P, ↑(EuclideanGeometry.distanceMultiplicity P u) ^ 2 ≤ C * ↑P.card ^ 3', '[{"url":"https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures/blob/59f30aa314ba225fcd9268723ce8291616df1ab0/FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/94.lean","kind":"artifact","locator_id":"native-1"},{"url":"https://google-deepmind.github.io/src/FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/%C2%AB94%C2%BB/","kind":"artifact","locator_id":"native-2"}]'::jsonb, '{"module":"FormalConjectures.ErdosProblems.«94»","subsets":"[]","category":"research solved","docstring":"Suppose $n$ points in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ determine a convex polygon and the set of distances between\nthem is $\\{u_1,\\ldots,u_t\\}$. Suppose $u_i$ appears as the distance between $f(u_i)$ many pairs of\npoints. Then\n$$\\sum_i f(u_i)^2 \\ll n^3.$$\n\nIn [Er97c] Erdős claims that Fishburn solved this, but gives no reference.\n","collection":"Erdős Problems","answer_kinds":"[]","subject_codes":"[\"5\",\"52\"]","subject_names":"[\"Combinatorics\",\"Convex and discrete geometry\"]","category_label":"Solved","collection_url":"https://www.erdosproblems.com","display_module":"FormalConjectures.ErdosProblems.94","file_first_added":"2026-08-03T12:50:51-04:00","formal_statement":"∃ C > 0,\n  ∀ (P : Finset (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2))),\n    EuclideanGeometry.ConvexIndep ↑P →\n      ∑ u ∈ EuclideanGeometry.distanceSet P, ↑(EuclideanGeometry.distanceMultiplicity P u) ^ 2 ≤ C * ↑P.card ^ 3","source_blob_root":"sha256:ba09a21af6257987afed3733e9edc737bfe4d1f132f1cb07ca6f5fe216337d3b","formal_proof_kind":"lean4","file_last_modified":"2026-08-04T16:05:54-04:00","formal_proof_locator":"https://github.com/plby/lean-proofs/blob/main/src/v4.29.1/ErdosProblems/Erdos94.lean","formal_proof_present":true,"formal_proof_sorry_free":false}'::jsonb, 'sha256:2c21bf0228620cf757da172aa510c45ffc56ae015e8e1d9d642b15debd4b59a8', 'sha256:00464b27aaa9dadf951ebe530269b8da32c854ac9586917b02cb532d7c3128ff', 'reference_only', 'sha256:8e6818318391cef5f071f4