      ↑(Erdos321.R N) ≤ 1 / Real.log 2 * Real.log^[r] ↑N * ↑N / Real.log ↑N * ∏ i ∈ Finset.Icc 3 r, Real.log^[i] ↑N', '[{"url":"https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures/blob/59f30aa314ba225fcd9268723ce8291616df1ab0/FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/321.lean","kind":"artifact","locator_id":"native-1"},{"url":"https://google-deepmind.github.io/src/FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/%C2%AB321%C2%BB/","kind":"artifact","locator_id":"native-2"}]'::jsonb, '{"module":"FormalConjectures.ErdosProblems.«321»","subsets":"[]","category":"research solved","docstring":"Let $R(N)$ be the maximal such size. Results of Bleicher and Erdős from [BlEr75] and [BlEr76b] imply that\n$$\nR(N) \\le \\frac{1}{\\log 2} \\log_r N \\left( \\frac{N}{\\log N} \\prod_{i=3}^{r} \\log_i N \\right),\n$$\nvalid for any $k \\ge 4$ with $\\log_k N \\ge k$ and any $r \\ge 1$ with $\\log_{2r} N \\ge 1$. (In these bounds $\\log_i n$ denotes the $i$-fold iterated logarithm.)\n\n[BlEr75] Bleicher, M. N. and Erdős, P., _The number of distinct subsums of $\\sum \\sb{1}\\spN\\,1/i$_. Math. Comp. (1975), 29-42.\n[BlEr76b] Bleicher, Michael N. and Erdős, Paul, _Denominators of Egyptian fractions. II_. Illinois J. Math. (1976), 598-613.\n","collection":"Erdős Problems","answer_kinds":"[]","subject_codes":"[\"11\"]","subject_names":"[\"Number theory\"]","category_label":"Solved","collection_url":"https://www.erdosproblems.com","display_module":"FormalConjectures.ErdosProblems.321","file_first_added":"2025-10-06T19:01:30+09:00","formal_statement":"∀ (N r : ℕ),\n  1 ≤ r →\n    1 ≤ Real.log^[2 * r] ↑N →\n      ↑(Erdos321.R N) ≤ 1 / Real.log 2 * Real.log^[r] ↑N * ↑N / Real.log ↑N * ∏ i ∈ Finset.Icc 3 r, Real.log^[i] ↑N","source_blob_root":"sha256:601d8486743aede6803feaaefc7bbb73f0aa8873d0296a6a1c5400fd86c32357","formal_proof_kind":null,"file_last_modified":"2026-07-17T01:28:26+02:00","formal_proof_locator":null,"formal_proof_present":false,"formal_proof_sorry_free":false}'::jsonb, 'sha256:a436226ae08ad6a5823139